    "explanation": "On 21\u202fMay\u202f2018 coffee futures jumped more than 100 points (+5.5% day\u2011over\u2011day). The move was attributed to two contemporaneous factors: (1) reports of cold weather and light frosts in Brazil\u2019s coffee\u2011growing regions, which raised concerns about supply (source: doc_3af188e9b60a9e88; source: doc_78f83ebc29d17391), and (2) a weakening of the U.S. dollar against the Brazilian real, which made coffee cheaper in foreign currency terms (source: doc_3af188e9b60a9e88). Earlier technical support and similar weather concerns were noted two days earlier, reinforcing the market\u2019s bullish stance (source: doc_caf61c1188bc0100).",
